{
  "abstract": "On the exceptional Piezas fibre with paired products $ac=-3/4$ and $bd=-8/9$, a cyclic five-entry source leaves two seventh-entry spokes unpaid. A natural additional rule asks that two specified entries be the regular fifths of a mixed quadruple. We prove that this rule has no ordinary rational realization, even when only four of the remaining individual square conditions are required. In classical cyclic coordinates its necessary trace equation factors into two lines and two cubics. The cubic components map, through an original-root half-trace identity, to a genus-three curve with exactly five rational points; an unconditional rank bound and Chabauty-Coleman calculation at $7$ certify the list. The lines lead to the genus-five cover on which $v^2-180$, $v^2-12v+164$ and $v^2+28v/3+36$ must all be squares. We prove that this cover has exactly its eight rational points at infinity. Three rank-one elliptic images give two quadratic-height equations at $13$. Explicit local balls certify all away-from-$13$ targets, an all-degree coefficient bound certifies the analytic tail, and exact simultaneous residue lifting leaves only infinity. The original genus-nine conic cover consequently has exactly sixteen boundary points. The supplement includes independent rational-arithmetic checks and all computational inputs. The methods are applications of established Chabauty and elliptic-height theory. The result excludes the stated extra completion rule, not unrestricted completions on this fibre or rational Diophantine septuples.",
